> > whether or not they are present at the dinner.
> >
> > The problem with {do'o} would be that the "others" it involves needn't
> > be other *Pharisees*, so I'd avoid it here.
>
> Changed and committed.
>
> > Yeah, I realized right after sending the mail. But in Luke 11:44, he
> > only addresses the Pharisees, not the teachers of the law, at least in
> > the versions I have. (though the chapter as a whole is about both groups)
>
> Manuscript variation. The majority, the Peshitta, and A have the phrase
> "scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites"; p45 and the rest of the manuscripts
> from
> Egypt, and therefore Nestle-Aland and UBS, omit it.
>
> Pierre
